			(property "Description" "6-pin header connection for use with the \"FTDI BASIC\" pinout - TARGET SIDE.\n\nAlso known as \"Arduino Serial Program Header\".\n\nIt is used to mate with our FTDI Basic serial programmers using the Arduino IDE.\n\nNote, this device has \"TARGET\" in the name. It is intended to be used on a design that contains a target micro-controller that you wish to program.\n\nThe \"sister\" device, named \"CABLE\" is inteneded to be used on a design that usually lives on the end of your USB cable and prvides the converter chip (FTDI232 or FTDI231x) to commnicate serial RX/TX.\n\nYou can populate with some of these:\n\nhttps://www.sparkfun.com/products/116  Break Away Headers - Straight (PRT-00116)\n\nFor reference (or to suit your programming needs) check out these designs:\n\n• https://www.sparkfun.com/products/9716  SparkFun FTDI Basic Breakout - 5V (DEV-09716)\n• https://www.sparkfun.com/products/9873  SparkFun FTDI Basic Breakout - 3.3V (DEV-09873)\n• https://www.sparkfun.com/products/12935  SparkFun FTDI SmartBasic (DEV-12935)\n• https://www.sparkfun.com/products/13746  SparkFun Beefy 3 - FTDI Basic Breakout (DEV-13746)"
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
			)
